{
  "format": "datadog-trace-v1.0-idx-msgpack",
  "description": "Fixtures for validating a v1.0 (idx) trace payload msgpack decoder. Every payload here was produced by the trace agent's reference encoder (pkg/proto/pbgo/trace/idx) using its inline string-streaming MarshalMsg, which is the encoding real tracers emit. Base64-decode payload_base64, decode it as a tracer payload, and compare the result against expected. Strings in expected are already resolved through the streaming-string table.",
  "notes": [
    "Attribute maps are encoded as a flat msgpack array whose length is 3x the number of entries (key, value type, value); the order of entries within one map is not significant.",
    "Strings are 'streaming strings': the first occurrence of a string is written inline as a msgpack string and appended to the decoder's string table (index 0 is always the empty string); later occurrences are written as a uint32 index into that table.",
    "These payloads do not carry an explicit string table (field 1 of the tracer payload) because this encoder never emits one. A decoder must still support that field.",
    "Field numbers are msgpack uint keys, and fields equal to their zero value are omitted, so map headers vary in size between cases."
  ],
  "cases": [
